+
+### Bug Fix: gear sell price ignored level scaling entirely (patch 0281)
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Bug Fix
+
+- Fixed: selling a piece of gear now actually pays out for how strong it rolled, not just its bone-stock template price
+- A high-level or Heroic/Legendary-tier drop that used to sell for pocket change now sells for something in line with what it'd cost to replace
+```
+
+Direct request: a full review of equipment sell values, prompted by
+gear now scaling with level (patch 0214's procedural rolls, patch
+0258's dedicated chain-replay/raid rewards) while sell price stayed
+completely blind to that. Audited every item in `equipment.json` (141
+total): 34 are blank procedural templates and 39 more are hand-authored
+chain/raid-exclusive rewards eligible for `scaleDedicatedItem`'s level
+scaling -- 73 items, over half the roster, whose real power can swing
+far above their authored `value` once dropped high-level, and every one
+of them was selling off that same low, stale number regardless.
+
+**Root cause, confirmed in `EquipmentManager.sellValue`:** it priced
+strictly off `def.value` -- the template's own low, unscaled authored
+number (a `wooden_sword`'s `value` is 2 gold) -- with no reference to
+`item.rolledItemLevel` at all. `shopPrice` got the equivalent fix back
+in patch 0241 for procedural templates specifically; sell price was
+never brought in line, and dedicated scaled items (patch 0258) never
+got it on either side.
+
+**Fix:** new `EquipmentManager.sellReferenceValue(item, def)` computes
+the "what's this worth new" baseline sellValue prices against --
+`shopPrice`'s own `shop.baseValuePerLevel * RARITY_PRICE_MULT[rarity] *
+(1 + rolledItemLevel * shop.valueGrowthPerLevelPercent / 100)` curve
+whenever `item.rolledItemLevel` is set, falling back to the item's
+plain authored `def.value` when it isn't (an ordinary fixed-power item,
+or a first-clear chain/raid grant with no roll info -- those were never
+stale to begin with). Deliberately keyed on `rolledItemLevel` being
+present rather than on `isProceduralTemplate` the way `shopPrice` is --
+gear scales via two separate mechanisms now, and a dedicated raid Set
+piece scaled up by `scaleDedicatedItem` deserves the same treatment as
+a procedural roll at the same level, not a worse deal for having come
+from the other path. `sellValue` itself is otherwise unchanged --
+condition (0.4-1.0 off current/max durability) and the existing
+`+plus` bonus (`1 + plus * 0.25`) still apply on top of the corrected
+reference, and the overall sell-vs-shop-price ratio (~30%) stays the
+same as before, it's just now anchored to the item's real worth instead
+of its template's.
+
+Every call site (`ShopManager.sell`, `ShopManager.sellBelowRarity`'s
+preview and batch, the Blacksmith's per-item Sell button/confirm text)
+already routes through `EquipmentManager.sellValue` with no duplicated
+math anywhere in the UI layer, so this one function change is the
+entire fix -- nothing else needed touching.
+
+**Noted but deliberately not touched in this patch:** `upgradeCost` has
+the identical shape of bug (`def.value * 0.6 * pow(1.65, plus)`, same
+blindness to `rolledItemLevel`), meaning Workshop upgrade cost on a
+high-level scaled item is currently underpriced the same way sell price
+was overpriced-low. Out of scope here since the ask was specifically
+about sell value -- flagged in Cleanup items below as a real follow-up,
+not forgotten.
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` passes clean against a fresh clone of
+current `main`. Confirmed via a standalone script that a level-50
+procedural Legendary template (e.g. a rolled Legendary sword) now sells
+for roughly what its shop-price curve says it should be worth at that
+level, instead of the few gold its unscaled template `value` used to
+yield. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- pricing math only, no change to
+`GameState`'s shape.
